### to the BRIDGE MASTER's PVID and br_fdb_find_rcu() searches the wrong VLAN -> miss -> walk fails ->
### flow never offloaded (silent software-forwarding fallback, NOT a black hole). 675-06 seeds ctx.vlan[0]
### + one info.encap[] entry from the packet's ingress VLAN (skb tag, else ingress-port PVID); ports that
### egress the VLAN untagged emit DEV_PATH_BR_VLAN_UNTAG and pop it again. Needs a ctx-taking walk, so it
### also splits + exports __dev_fill_forward_path() in net/core/dev.c (the half we deliberately dropped
### from the old 675-01 - it is now load-bearing). PVID/untagged br-lan flows are behaviour-IDENTICAL
### (TAG->KEEP/push before vs KEEP->pop/none after = same encap count, same wire format), so no risk to
### existing users; only non-PVID VLAN flows change, and those are not offloaded at all today.
