### 747: re-trigger the JCPLL VCO band search on the AN7581 ETH lane (10G lan2 -> RTL8261N over USXGMII).
### Root cause from an openwrt-forum W1700K post (same 2x RTL8261N board as ours): the driver programs
### JCPLL_VCO_TCLVAR (pcs_ana+0x30 bits[2:0]) ONCE in an7581_pcs_jcpll_bringup(), BEFORE it enables the PLL,
### and never rewrites it — so the band search runs with the PLL off and can settle on a VCO code the PHY's
### system-side SerDes cannot lock onto (SoC TX -> PHY RX): no block lock, USXGMII in-band AN never completes,
### lane dead forever (poster: 0/100 link-ups). A TCLVAR *transition* with the PLL already running re-runs the
### search onto a good code — final value is irrelevant (0x3 and 0x5 both work), only the change matters.
### Fix adds a post_config op to struct airoha_pcs_match_data, called at the END of airoha_pcs_config() (after
### bringup + airoha_pcs_init + USXGMII AN enable — end of an7581_pcs_bringup is too early), and wires it into
### an7581_pcs_eth ONLY (USXGMII/10GBASER); PON/WAN lane (an7581_pcs_pon) untouched. Complements 745/746
### (those fix the SoC-RX manual calib; this fixes the SoC-TX/JCPLL side — different layer). 3 files
### (pcs-airoha.h/.c-an7581/-common), dry-run applies clean (0 fuzz/0 offset). ⚠️ VERIFIED ON ONE BOARD ONLY
### (the poster's, which was 100% dead) — our lan2 currently WORKS, so this is a SOAK candidate that touches a
### working lane: harmless-when-correct per the poster, but confirm with the live devmem test before relying on
### it — `devmem 0x1fa7a030` (dead=0x0000301B) then `devmem 0x1fa7a030 32 0x0000301D`. Possible fix for our
### intermittent lan2 issues. See [[project_w1700k_lan2_rx]] / [[project_w1700k_hw11_lan2_hang]].
